<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korean firms buy 52,000T U.S. No.3 corn.</title>
<headline>S.Korean firms buy 52,000T U.S. No.3 corn.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1996-09-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korean feed mill companies, including Sunjin Co Ltd, bought late Thursday 52,000 tonnes of U.S. No.3 corn at $159.18 a tonne, C&amp;F, traders said.  </p>
<p>Traders said on Friday that Toepfer won the contract. Shipment was set on seller's option for May 8-27 if from the U.S. Gulf, or for May 27-June 15 if from the Pacific Northwest.</p>
<p>Arrival was set to the western port city of Inchon.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5651</p>
</text>
